Z||000000||iplayazi||05-25-2000||01:28 AM||||I have an 87 gt and lately it hasn't been running very smoothly lately. Ive changed the oil a few weeks ago with synthetic oil, I put the injector cleaner periodically with premium gas. The plugs been changed with the rotor and wires. It has a bit of a rough idle. Ive got the battery going lower when my signals click or when I turn on the a/c, but thats been happening since I bought the car 4 years ago. Is there anything that I could service or replace? Thanks for the space. Anyhelp is appreciated!||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phaeton||05-25-2000||03:13 AM||||How old is the battery itself?  Does it barely have enough juice to start the Fiero?  A marginal battery can throw the electric system off a little, everything tries to run off the alternator and surges aren't adequately backed up with battery power so the voltage gives momentary drops.<P>My igloo battery has a short life here in Alaska.<P>Not knowing how many miles or how they were put on, but when the compression starts to go the first place it shows up is in erratic idle.  More air gets past worn rings when the engine is moving slow, takes a couple extra turns to start and smooths out very slowly.<P>I wanna ask about spark strength but nothing was said about high speed roughness so I won't.||||reg||12
